      "tip": "The tens: **দশ (10), বিশ (20), ত্রিশ (30), চল্লিশ (40), পঞ্চাশ (50), ষাট (60), সত্তর (70), আশি (80), নব্বই (90), একশ (100).**\n\nHonest warning: **every number from 21 to 99 has its own form** (একুশ 21, বাইশ 22, … নিরানব্বই 99). Don't try to learn them all at once — the tens let you understand most prices and ages roughly, and you'll pick up the rest by use.\n\n**সাত** (7) and **ষাট** (60) are both transliterated *shat*; the difference is in the 't' sound (curled tongue in ষাট). Listen to the audio!\n\nBig numbers: **হাজার** = 1,000, **লাখ** (*lakh*) = 100,000, **কোটি** (*koti*) = 10 million. South Asia counts in lakhs and crores, so ১,০০,০০০ is written with commas that way.",
